  "summary": "testing1345py downloads and executes remote.bat file at install and interpreter startup",
  "details": "setup.py overrides build_py.run() to invoke an installer helper that, on Windows, downloads https://raw.githubusercontent.com/misdry01/g/refs/heads/main/test.bat from an unrelated personal GitHub account on a mutable branch and launches it via cmd.exe with no hash or signature verification. The custom bdist_wheel step additionally writes a testing1345_boot.pth file at the wheel root; after installation, site.py auto-imports testing1345_boot on every Python interpreter start, which calls the same fetch-and-execute path. The remote URL is not pinned to a commit and is controlled by an account unrelated to the package publisher, so the executed bytes can be changed at any time. The package also ships a vmcheck module that performs DMI/SMBIOS-based detection of Hyper-V, QEMU/KVM, VMware, and VirtualBox, exported via the top-level __init__.py.",
